[7.67782, "o", "{\r\n    \"1\": {\r\n        \"origin_input\": \"The poem Iliad is frequently described as a masculine or heroic epic, especially compared with the Odyssey.\",\r\n        \"Multi_Hop\": {\r\n            \"declare_input\": \"The poem Iliad, attributed to Homer, traditionally said to be the inventor of the Greek alphabet and the author of the Iliad and the Odyssey and revered as the greatest of ancient Greek epic poets whose historicity is still subject to academic debate, and set during the Trojan War focusing on the hero Achilles and his anger towards King Agamemnon, is frequently described as a masculine or heroic epic, especially compared with the Odyssey.\",\r\n            \"declare_ans\": {\r\n                \"GPT3\": \"The Iliad, an ancient epic of renown,\\nIts authorship attributed to Homer alone,\\nDebated by scholars, its historicity unclear,\\nYet its influence endures, for many hold it dear.\\n\\nSet in the time of the Trojan War's grim strife,\\nWhere heroes clashed, battling for their life,\\nAchilles, the mighty warrior, takes ce"]
[7.677982, "o", "nter stage,\\nHis anger towards Agamemnon fuels the rage.\\n\\nThis poem, often described as masculine and grand,\\nWith its themes of war and heroism, does stand,\\nIn contrast to the Odyssey, its companion piece,\\nWhich focuses on the journey and the search for peace.\\n\\nThe Iliad evokes the image of heroes bold,\\nWarriors fierce, their stories often told,\\nIt celebrates their valor, their strength, and might,\\nIn vivid detail, it depicts the glory of the fight.\\n\\nThough it may seem to lean towards a certain mold,\\nWith its emphasis on masculinity so bold,\\nThe Iliad's power lies in its timeless appeal,\\nIts exploration of human nature, both raw and real.\\n\\nFor even today, its themes resonate,\\nAs we contemplate the impacts of war and hate,\\nThe Iliad, a testament to the human heart,\\nIts tales of heroes and honor, a timeless art.\",\r\n                \"GPT4\": {\r\n                    \"answer\": \"The Iliad is indeed an epic poem, attributed to the ancient Greek poet Homer. While Homer is traditionally said to have c"]
[7.678062, "o", "omposed both the Iliad and the Odyssey and sometimes is credited with the creation of the Greek alphabet, most scholars now believe that the alphabet existed before Homer's time and that the works are likely to be the product of a long oral tradition. The Iliad is known for its focus on heroic action and the valor of warriors like Achilles during the Trojan War. It contrasts with the Odyssey, which is more focused on the cleverness and versatility of its hero, Odysseus, and has a broader thematic scope, including elements of romance and homecoming. The historicity of Homer and the events of the Iliad are still debated in academic circles. The poem's themes of anger, honor, and heroism, embodied by Achilles' relationship with King Agamemnon, resonate with the traditional concepts of masculinity in ancient Greek culture.\",\r\n                    \"relatedLinks\": [\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"The Iliad | Summary, Characters, & Facts\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https:"]
[7.678524, "o", "//www.britannica.com/topic/Iliad\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Was Homer a historical figure?\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.history.com/news/was-homer-a-historical-figure\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Greek Alphabet - History and Development\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.ancient.eu/Greek_Alphabet/\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"The Oral Tradition of the Iliad\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/classical-quarterly/article/abs/oral-tradition-of-homers-iliad/8FAFBF310E389B67F554102A88DB409D\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Achilles: The Ancient Greek Hero from the Iliad\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.ancient.eu/Achilles/\"\r\n                        },\r\n      "]
[7.678624, "o", "                  {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Trojan War Mythology and History\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.worldhistory.org/Trojan_War/\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Masculinity and the Warrior Culture of The Iliad\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://digitalcommons.trinity.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?referer=&httpsredir=1&article=1169&context=classics_honors\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"title\": \"Compare and Contrast: The Iliad vs. The Odyssey\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.sparknotes.com/lit/iliad/essay/a/\"\r\n                        }\r\n                    ]\r\n                },\r\n                \"ppai\": {\r\n                    \"text\": \"The poem Iliad, attributed to Homer, is frequently described as a masculine or heroic epic, especially compared with the Odyssey. It portrays a society where men held higher positions than women, who"]
[7.67886, "o", " were often treated more like objects than people[1][2][3][4]. In Homer's time, men supported the families and protected them because their role was more dominant, while women were rarely considered their own individuals but always an extension of their husband, father, or brother[4]. The portrayal of women in The Iliad reflects the societal norms of ancient Greece, where women were taught to accept the rules of men in authority above them because they lacked the same rights as males[4]. The role of females in The Iliad is depicted as demoting and inferior to men, with women being treated like slaves and property rather than human beings[4]. The poem centers on the brutality and gruesome aspect of war, making it difficult to visualize any room for the tenderness of women when it comes to battle, although they play a crucial role behind the scenes by supporting and giving advice to the warriors[4]. Therefore, The Iliad is often seen as reinforcing traditional gender roles and portraying women in a subordinate "]
[7.678976, "o", "position to men.\",\r\n                    \"sources\": [\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"0\": {\r\n                                \"name\": \"Gender Roles in The Iliad - Video & Lesson Transcript | Study.com\",\r\n                                \"url\": \"https://study.com/academy/lesson/gender-roles-in-the-iliad.html\"\r\n                            }\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"1\": {\r\n                                \"name\": \"Gender Stereotypes in The Iliad: Analysis of Thetis and Achilles - Free Essay Example\",\r\n                                \"url\": \"https://edubirdie.com/examples/gender-stereotypes-in-the-iliad-analysis-of-thetis-and-achilles/\"\r\n                            }\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"2\": {\r\n                                \"name\": \"THE PORTRAYAL OF WOMEN IN THE ILIAD - jstor\",\r\n                                \"url\": \"https://www.jstor.org/stable/24591564\"\r\n           "]
[7.679479, "o", "                 }\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"3\": {\r\n                                \"name\": \"Gender Roles in \\\"The Iliad\\\" by Homer: [Essay Example], 1430 words GradesFixer\",\r\n                                \"url\": \"https://gradesfixer.com/free-essay-examples/gender-roles-in-in-the-iliad-by-homer/\"\r\n                            }\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"4\": {\r\n                                \"name\": \"The Objectification Of Women In Homer's The Iliad - IPL.org\",\r\n                                \"url\": \"https://www.ipl.org/essay/The-Objectification-Of-Women-In-Homers-The-F3GWZM7EACPR\"\r\n                            }\r\n                        }\r\n                    ]\r\n                },\r\n                \"youchat\": {\r\n                    \"answer\": \"Yes, Homer is traditionally attributed as the author of the Iliad and the Odyssey, two major ancient Greek epic poems. He is considered one of the great"]
[7.679586, "o", "est ancient Greek epic poets and is revered for his contributions to literature.\",\r\n                    \"links\": [\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"ai_snippets\": \"The Iliad (\\\"a poem about Ilium (Troy)\\\") is one of two major ancient Greek epic poems attributed to Homer. It is one of the oldest extant works of literature still widely read by modern audiences. As with the Odyssey, the poem is divided into 24 books and was written in dactylic hexameter. It contains 15,693 lines in its most widely accepted version. Set towards the end of the Trojan War, a ten-year siege of the city of Troy by a coalition of Mycenaean Greek states, the poem depicts significant events in the siege's final weeks. In particular, it depicts a fierce quarrel between King Agamemnon and a celebrated warrior, Achilles. It is a central part of the Epic Cycle. The Iliad is often regarded as the first substantial piece of European literature. The Iliad and the Odyssey were likely written down in Homeric Greek, a liter"]
[7.679758, "o", "ary amalgam of Ionic Greek and other dialects, probably around the late 8th or early 7th century BC. Homer's authorship was infrequently questioned in antiquity, but\",\r\n                            \"description\": \"The Iliad (/ˈɪliəd/; Ancient Greek: Ἰλιάς, romanized: Iliás, Attic Greek: [iː.li.ás]; &quot;a poem about Ilium (Troy)&quot;) is one of two major ancient Greek epic poems attributed to Homer. It is one of the oldest extant works of literature still widely read by modern audiences. As with the Odyssey, the poem is divided into 24 books and was written in dactylic hexameter. It contains 15,693 lines in its most widely accepted version. Set towards the end of the Trojan War, a ten-year siege of the city of Troy by a coalition of Mycenaean Greek states, the poem depicts significant events in the siege&#x27;s final weeks.\",\r\n                            \"snippet\": \"The Iliad (\\\"a poem about Ilium (Troy)\\\") is one of two major ancient Greek epic poems attributed to Homer. It is one of the oldest "]
[7.67988, "o", "extant works of literature still widely read by modern audiences. As with the Odyssey, the poem is divided into 24 books and was written in dactylic hexameter. It contains 15,693 lines in its most widely accepted version. Set towards the end of the Trojan War, a ten-year siege of the city of Troy by a coalition of Mycenaean Greek states, the poem depicts significant events in the siege's final weeks. In particular, it depicts a fierce quarrel between King Agamemnon and a celebrated warrior, Achilles. It is a central part of the Epic Cycle. The Iliad is often regarded as the first substantial piece of European literature. The Iliad and the Odyssey were likely written down in Homeric Greek, a literary amalgam of Ionic Greek and other dialects, probably around the late 8th or early 7th century BC. Homer's authorship was infrequently questioned in antiquity, but\",\r\n                            \"title\": \"Iliad - Wikipedia\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliad\"\r\n                 "]
[7.679898, "o", "       },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"ai_snippets\": \"Homer, (flourished 9th or 8th century bce, Ionia?), ancient Greek poet, presumed author of the Iliad and the Odyssey. Though almost nothing is known of his life, tradition holds that Homer was blind. The ancient Greeks attributed to him the great epic poems the Iliad and the Odyssey. Modern scholars generally agree that he composed (but was not the original creator of) the Iliad, most likely relying on oral traditions, and at least inspired the composition of the Odyssey.\\nThe Iliad, set during the Trojan War, tells the story of the wrath of Achilles. The Odyssey tells the story of Odysseus as he travels home from the war. The two epics provided the basis of Greek education and culture in the Classical age, and they have remained among the most significant poems of the European tradition. The method of their composition has been long debated.\",\r\n                            \"description\": \"<strong>Homer, (flourished 9th or 8th ce"]
[7.679937, "o", "ntury bce, Ionia?), ancient Greek poet, presumed author of the Iliad and the Odyssey</strong>. Though almost nothing is known of his life, tradition holds that Homer was blind. The ancient Greeks attributed to him the great epic poems the Iliad and the Odyssey.\",\r\n                            \"snippet\": \"Homer, (flourished 9th or 8th century bce, Ionia?), ancient Greek poet, presumed author of the Iliad and the Odyssey. Though almost nothing is known of his life, tradition holds that Homer was blind. The ancient Greeks attributed to him the great epic poems the Iliad and the Odyssey. Modern scholars generally agree that he composed (but was not the original creator of) the Iliad, most likely relying on oral traditions, and at least inspired the composition of the Odyssey.\\nThe Iliad, set during the Trojan War, tells the story of the wrath of Achilles. The Odyssey tells the story of Odysseus as he travels home from the war. The two epics provided the basis of Greek education and culture in the Classical age, an"]
[7.679952, "o", "d they have remained among the most significant poems of the European tradition. The method of their composition has been long debated.\",\r\n                            \"title\": \"Homer and the epic poems the Iliad and the Odyssey | Britannica\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/summary/Homer-Greek-poet\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"ai_snippets\": \"Analysis\\nAlthough attributed to Homer, “The Iliad” is clearly dependent on an older oral tradition and may well have been the collective inheritance of many singer-poets over a long period of time (the historical Fall of Troy is usually dated to around the start of the 12th Century BCE). Homer was probably one of the first generation of authors who were also literate, as the Greek alphabet was introduced in the early 8th Century BCE. We knows this because the language used in his epic poems is an archaic version of Ionic Greek, with admixtures from certain other dialects such as"]
[7.680205, "o", " Aeolic Greek. However, it is by no means certain that Homer himself (if in fact such a man ever really existed) actually wrote down the verses.\",\r\n                            \"description\": \"Who wrote <strong>the</strong> <strong>iliad</strong> ✅ A basic level guide to some of the best known and loved works of prose, poetry and drama from <strong>ancient</strong> Greece ✅ <strong>The</strong> <strong>Iliad</strong> <strong>by</strong> <strong>Homer</strong>\",\r\n                            \"snippet\": \"Analysis\\nAlthough attributed to Homer, “The Iliad” is clearly dependent on an older oral tradition and may well have been the collective inheritance of many singer-poets over a long period of time (the historical Fall of Troy is usually dated to around the start of the 12th Century BCE). Homer was probably one of the first generation of authors who were also literate, as the Greek alphabet was introduced in the early 8th Century BCE. We knows this because the language used in his epic poems is an archaic"]
[7.680881, "o", " version of Ionic Greek, with admixtures from certain other dialects such as Aeolic Greek. However, it is by no means certain that Homer himself (if in fact such a man ever really existed) actually wrote down the verses.\",\r\n                            \"title\": \"THE ILIAD - HOMER - POEM: STORY, SUMMARY & ANALYSIS\",\r\n                            \"url\": \"https://ancient-literature.com/greece_homer_iliad/\"\r\n                        },\r\n                        {\r\n                            \"ai_snippets\": \"The Iliad by Homer – Poem: Story, Summary & Analysis\\n(Epic Poem, Greek, c. 750 BCE, 15,693 lines\\nIntroduction | Synopsis | Analysis | Resources\\nIntroduction – Who wrote the Iliad\\n“The Iliad“ (Gr: “Iliás“) is an epic poem by the ancient Greek poet Homer, which recounts some of the significant events of the final weeks of the Trojan War and the Greek siege of the city of Troy (which was also known as Ilion, Ilios or Ilium in ancient times). Written in the mid-8th Century BCE, “The Iliad” is usua"]
[7.680975, "o", "lly considered to be the earliest work in the whole Western literary tradition, and one of the best known and loved stories of all time.\\nThrough its portrayal of the Trojan War, the stirring scenes of bloody battle, the wrath of Achilles and the constant interventions of the gods, it explores themes of glory, wrath, homecoming and fate. Moreover, the Homeric epic has provided subjects and stories for many other later Greek, Roman, and Renaissance writings.\\nSynopsis – Iliad Summary\",\r\n                            \"description\": \"Who wrote <strong>the</strong> <strong>iliad</strong> ✅ A basic level guide to some of the best known and loved works of prose, poetry and drama from <strong>ancient</strong> Greece ✅ <strong>The</strong> <strong>Iliad</strong> <strong>by</strong> <strong>Homer</strong>\",\r\n                            \"snippet\": \"The Iliad by Homer – Poem: Story, Summary & Analysis\\n(Epic Poem, Greek, c. 750 BCE, 15,693 lines\\nIntroduction | Synopsis | Analysis | Resources\\nIntroduction – Who"]
[7.681178, "o", " wrote the Iliad\\n“The Iliad“ (Gr: “Iliás“) is an epic poem by the ancient Greek poet Homer, which recounts some of the significant events of the final weeks of the Trojan War and the Greek siege of the city of Troy (which was also known as Ilion, Ilios or Ilium in ancient times). Written in the mid-8th Century BCE, “The Iliad” is usually considered to be the earliest work in the whole Western literary tradition, and one of the best known and loved stories of all time.\\nThrough its portrayal of the Trojan War, the stirring scenes of bloody battle, the wrath of Achilles and the constant interventions of the gods, it explores themes of glory, wrath, homecoming and fate. Moreover,\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32magent@95c8f7f39f57\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
